Hi Christina,

What are you assigning to the columns, exactly? The HDOP column should be sqrt(2) * standard_deviation of the errors in in each dimension to get an RMS UERE of 1. Without the sqrt(2), you should get an RMS UERE of 1.41.
Is this with a recent version of the package, and can you provide me with a minimal working example (data + script) to look at? I'm not really sure what's going on from looking at things.

Best,
Chris

