I did not multiply by sqrt(2) for the HDOP column, so I guess that explains why the estimated UERE was ~1.3 - assuming that only a perfect prediction would produce 1.41 exactly. I'll email you a zip file that contains the UERE that resulted from that HDOP assignment without the sqrt(2), the bighorn data I used in this example with that UERE already assigned, and the code I used to try both approaches and compare model fits. If you need the stationary data too, let me know and I can send that along as well. As always, extremely thankful for you to take a look at this and let me know if I screwed anything up here or if this odd variogram suggests something flawed with the model.

Christina

